                <pb facs="0580" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg468"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Fox to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-06-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 6,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Ecuadorian Congress, June 2, conferred extraordinary powers upon the Executive
                    under article 83 of the constitution. June 4 the following executive decree
                    issued and first published this evening: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The only article as follows: The army continues in the state of campaign.
                            Minister of war is charged with execution of this decree.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">(Signed.) <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alfaro</hi> and
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Martinez Aguirre.</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Opinion is that action taken is precautionary, due to the rumor of internal
                    uneasiness.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
